andling it now for those of you who are  not aware  wakanda and atlantis which is where  neymar is from have  a very long history together and a very  big  rivalry now when they said this in  avengers in-game a lot of people  immediately thought  atlantis the earthquake was caused by  neymar and his  people and akoyi most likely doesn't  want everybody to know about the  atlanteans  after all wakanda was kept a secret to  everybody for many many years they  probably don't want word of atlantis  getting out but this easter egg was  never confirmed until the other day  a few days ago christopher marcus and  steven mcfeely the writers for avengers  in-game took over comicbook.com's  twitter account during a quarantine  watch party  and during this time they did a q a they  took some questions from fans on twitter  in which one person asked was a koi's  message about dealing with underwater  tremors by  leaving it alone a direct reference to  atlantis and  namor in which christopher marcus  replied sometimes you plant seeds  sometimes they grow and this is  definitely a confirmation if it was not  an easter egg they would have simply  said no  they have said no to questions like  these in the past before they would have  simply said no  again instead they confirmed that they  planted a  seed and it's growing and that seed is  namor and his introduction to the mcu  now namor coming to the mcu was pretty  much inevitable as we had it  especially with black panther and the  introduction of wakanda to the mcu  not to mention the x-men are coming and  the fantastic four as well and namor has  a big connection to  both of those groups and as i mentioned  before there's a rumor going around that  namor is going to be appearing  in three films first to appear in the  eternals which we've had a report for  in the past already then appearing again  in doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness until finally debuting in black  panther 2 as the main antagonist of the  film  now like i said it's just a rumor for  now however we have had  individual reports in the past that have  said that namor is going to show up  in the eternals along with his city  atlantis and then we have also had a  report that he's going to show up  in doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness and as far as him showing up as  the villain in black panther 2 story  wise it makes the most sense but let's  talk about his first appearances  in the mcu as rumored the first report  that we got for neymor was that he is  going to be  appearing in the eternals film and  atlantis is going to be appearing as  well what it's supposed to show  is apparently the sinking of atlantis  this makes a lot of sense to show and  tease in the eternals because the  eternals are essentially  immortal beings they live for thousands  and thousands of years and  the eternal's film is going to show them  over various different points throughout  their lives  and it's already been confirmed by  various different set photos that the  eternals are going to  visit the ancient egyptian and ancient  mayan times we have leaked photos from  the set that  show the tomb of the space gods and the  report is is when the eternals are  back in that era in the film they're  going to show the seeking of atlantis  now the avengers in-game easter egg is  not the only name or easter egg that  we've had in the mcu there was actually  one in iron man 2.  in a scene in iron man 2 where tony  stark is speaking with nick fury there's  a hologram in the back with a world  map on it on the map there are several  locations that are marked one  is wakanda and at this point wakanda had  not really been mentioned the only thing  that had been mentioned was  vibranium but there's another mark that  is right next to wakanda  in the middle of the atlantic ocean and  there's only one thing that could be  right off the coast of africa in the  middle of the atlantic ocean and that  is atlantis now at the time there were  plans f